    <DataNode elementId="AT1G78510-MONOMER" textLabel="Solanesyl pyrophosphate synthase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8S948" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana SPS1&lt;/i&gt; gene was shown to encode a protein with polyprenyl diphosphate synthase activity |CITS:[12437513],[15653808]|. This was assessed both by phenotypical complementation of the &lt;i&gt;Schizosaccharomyces pombe&lt;/i&gt; mutant strain &amp;Delta;&lt;i&gt;dps1&lt;/i&gt; and &amp;Delta;&lt;i&gt;dls1&lt;/i&gt; |CITS:[15653808]| (note that the recombinant protein was a 45-aminoacid mitochondrial targeting signal from Ppt1, which is known to be located in the mitochondria) and the purification and assay of a recombinant form of the protein |CITS:[12437513]|. In the latter experiment, it was shown that the enzyme can use FPP or GGPP as substrate and catalyzes the formation of a variety of polyprenyl diphosphate products ranging from C&lt;sub&gt;25&lt;/sub&gt; (|FRAME:GERANYLGERANYL-PP|) to C&lt;sub&gt;45&lt;/sub&gt; (|FRAME: SOLANESYL-PYROPHOSPHATE|) (SPP) but the majority is released as SPP especially when |FRAME:GERANYLGERANYL-PP GGPP| is used as the substrate |CITS:[12437513]|. Further enzyme characterization demonstrated that |FRAME:GERANYLGERANYL-PP GGPP| is preferred as a substrate over FPP |CITS:[12437513]|. |FRAME: ORG-5993| possesses two isozymes that catalyze the same reaction. |FRAME: AT1G17050| supplies the precursor of the plastoquinone side-chain, while |FRAME: AT1G78510| contributes to the biosynthesis of the ubiquinone side-chain |CITS: [15784989]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G78510-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G78510.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q8S948" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AtSPS1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="All-trans-nonaprenyl-diphosphate synthase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="geranylgeranyl-diphosphate specific)" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33221, RXN-12893, RXN-12892, RXN-12891, RXN-12889, RXN-17877, RXN-ARA-188, RXN-9617, RXN-9616" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="9" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005783" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G78510.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G78510" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="15653808" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCO-ER" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12437513" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15653808" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15784989" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT3G11945-MONOMER" textLabel="homogentisate solanesyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G11945-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">This enzyme functions as a homogentisate prenyltransferase when expressed heterologously in membrane fractions of &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; with an enzymatic activity of 5 pmol min&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; mg&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; protein |CITS: [16989822]|. This enzyme works best with homogentisate as a prenyl acceptor. Under initial experimental conditions, the protein seemed to have the highest activity with farnesyl diphosphate and geranylgeranyl diphosphate. However, the addition of of 0.12 mM n-dodecyl b-D-maltoside significantly increased the activity of the enzyme toward solanesyl diphosphate (SDP), most likely because this detergent solubilized the long chain SDP compound |CITS: [16989822]|. Based on studies of HST from &lt;i&gt;Chlamydomonas reinhardtii&lt;/i&gt;, spinach, and Arabidopsis, a model for the mechanism of this enzyme has been proposed. It is hypothesized the HST binds to prenyl diphosphate in distinct manners to form at least two alternative complexes that go on to react differently with homogentisate and prenylate it prior to or after it becomes decarboxylated. It is also supposed that the larger |FRAME: SOLANESYL-PYROPHOSPHATE SDP|substrate binds tightly and preferentially in the mode that favors prenylation with decarboxylation. |CITS: [20400515]|. Overexpression of this HST enzyme in Arabidopsis plants causes increased accumuation of plastoquinone-9 and, surprisingly, tocochromanols (primarily &amp;alpha;-tocopherol). While the former is likely due to the activity of HST with SDP, directly upstream of plastoquinone-9 biosynthesis, the effect of HST on tocopherol accumulation is hypothesized to be indirect |CITS: [16989822]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G11945-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33307, RXN-12698" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009941" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G11945.2" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G11945" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="17569077" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOR-ENV-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16989822" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_20400515" />
    </DataNode>
