    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-3261" textLabel="MONOMER-3261" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-3261" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The vte3 mutant plants have a significant decrease in alpha and gamma-tocopherol content, and an increase of beta and delta-tocopherol content. It provided genetic evidence that the vte3 locus is responsible for the MPBQ methyltransferase activity and is involved in tocopherol biosynthesis. In addition, plastoquinone level is also significantly decreased in the vte3 mutants which indicates that vte3 is also involved in plastoquinone biosynthesis. Vte3 was expressed in E.coli and in-vitro assay demonstrated that it encodes the MPBQ/MSBQ methyltransferase and the enzyme uses both MPBQ and MSBQ as substrates.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-3261" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="MPBQ/MSBQ methyltransferase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-22132, RXN-12804, RXN-3421, RXN-3841" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
